      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #45812.\n\n`PrefillAdder.preempt_to_schedule` fills `preempt_list` by iterating a set of `Req` objects. `Req` hashes by `id()`, so that order follows object addresses and can differ between TP ranks. The scheduler requeues the victims in `preempt_list` order. That order stamps their `wait_queue_entry_time`, which the priority queue sort and the next victim selection both read; with `--max-queued-requests` it also decides which victim is aborted when the queue is full, and with HiCache storage it sets the order of the prefetch hit-count all-reduces. So when one preemption takes two or more victims, the ranks can go on to build different batches. Details and a CPU reproduction are in the issue. The set has been there since priority preemption was added (#8746).\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `preempt_to_schedule` keeps the set only for the membership test while releasing victims, and extends `preempt_list` from the ordered victim list, reversed: preferred priority first, then the earliest queued. This is the order of the default `fcfs` waiting queue, so the new `wait_queue_entry_time` stamps keep the victims' relative order. Selection order would requeue the most recently queued victim first and put the oldest one first in line for the next preemption.\n- Which requests are preempted, the threshold, the token accounting and the release order (`running_batch.reqs` order) do not change. The dLLM scheduler mixin consumes `preempt_list` the same way and gets the same order.\n\nRelated: #45686 adds preemption when KV runs out, where one preemption is more likely to take several victims. The two PRs touch different files.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `test_preempt_list_order_independent_of_req_hashes` in `test/registered/unit/managers/test_prefill_adder.py`: five running requests are preempted under two different `__hash__` assignments, standing in for two ranks, with both values of `--schedule-low-priority-values-first`, and `preempt_list` must come out in waiting-queue order every time. On `main` all four cases fail (`['c', 'a', 'e', 'b', 'd']` and `['d', 'b', 'e', 'a', 'c']` instead of `['a', 'b', 'c', 'd', 'e']`). They also fail if the list is extended in selection order or in `running_batch.reqs` order, and the `True` cases fail if the requeue order ignores the priority direction.\n- `test_prefill_adder.py`, `test_schedule_policy.py` and `test_retraction_order.py` pass locally (69 tests), and `pre-commit run` on the changed files is clean.\n- The reproduction script from the issue prints `['r0', 'r1', 'r2', 'r3', 'r4']` on every run with this change.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [x] No documentation change needed: preemption behavior as documented does not change.\n- [x] Accuracy and speed benchmarks are not applicable: no model code changes, and the set is still built once per preemption.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39774471228](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39774471228)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39774471131](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39774471131)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39774471220](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39774471220)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
